SheShield Companion
SheShield Companion is a connected personal-safety system that combines an ESP32 wearable, a React Native mobile app, GPS location sharing, emergency SMS, and a consent-based live camera session for trusted assistance.

The project is designed to help a user send an emergency alert quickly while sharing useful context with an authorized contact. The system supports Bluetooth Low Energy telemetry from a wearable, phone-based location capture, a configured SMS alert, and an authenticated web viewer for a temporary LiveKit session.

Safety notice: SheShield is a prototype and should not be treated as a replacement for local emergency services. Test the hardware, phone permissions, network coverage, SMS delivery, and trusted-viewer access before relying on it.

Main Features
•	Manual SOS: The user can trigger an emergency event from the mobile app or connected wearable.
•	Emergency SMS: The configured alert flow sends an SOS message to 8825542451 with the freshest available GPS coordinates and a Google Maps link.
•	Wearable telemetry: The app connects to an ESP32 wearable over BLE using a UART-style service.
•	Sensor support: The reference hardware supports motion, pulse/PPG contact quality, GPS, battery, and GSM fallback components.
•	Live location: The app requests location permission and attaches coordinates to the emergency alert when available.
•	Consented live camera: After an SOS event, the user must explicitly approve camera access before a LiveKit video session starts.
•	Authenticated viewer: A trusted viewer signs in and receives a short-lived subscriber token for the active SOS room.
•	Visible streaming state: The app shows when camera sharing is active and provides a stop control.
•	Event history: Emergency and wearable events can be reviewed in the app.
•	Contacts and settings: The app includes screens for contacts, connection preferences, permissions, and safety settings.
•	GSM fallback: The hardware documentation includes SIM800L-based SMS fallback for situations where the phone or internet path is unavailable.

